\fIdrop_duplicates, merge, value_counts\fR
.IX Subsection "drop_duplicates, merge, value_counts"
.PP
These three decide what counts as the same row, the same join key, or the same
value by a cell\*(Aqs Perl stringification, and on numeric columns that one
conversion was most of the work they did.
.PP
\&\f(CWsv_2pv_flags()\fR renders an NV with \f(CW\*(C`snprintf("%.*g", NV_DIG, x)\*(C'\fR, about 140 ns
a cell, and — unlike the IV case, where \f(CW\*(C`SvPOK_or_cached_IV\*(C'\fR lets the \f(CW\*(C`SvPV\*(C'\fR
macros hand back the string perl cached on the SV — it never reuses that PV, so
every pass over a column of doubles paid the conversion again. It does leave the
buffer behind, which is why keying a frame used to grow the caller\*(Aqs own numeric
columns by about 64 bytes a cell, permanently: reading a frame ought to be a
read.
.PP
\&\f(CWnk_num_pv()\fR now renders bare integers and bare doubles into the caller\*(Aqs own
scratch buffer instead, and leaves the SV untouched. Its double path is \f(CW\*(C`%.15g\*(C'\fR
about four times faster than the C library\*(Aqs, and taken only where the answer is
provably the same: the magnitude is scaled into \f(CW\*(C`[1e14, 1e15)\*(C'\fR in \f(CW\*(C`long double\*(C'\fR —
64 mantissa bits against the double\*(Aqs 53 — which bounds the scaled value\*(Aqs error
under 2e\-4, so a fractional part further than 2e\-3 from one half rounds exactly
as the true value would. About one cell in 300 lands nearer than that and goes
back through \f(CW\*(C`SvPV\*(C'\fR, as do zero, the non\-finite values, \f(CW\*(C`use locale\*(C'\fR, an x87
control word left at double precision, and any build whose NV is not an IEEE
double. It agreed with the C library\*(Aqs own \f(CW\*(C`%.15g\*(C'\fR over 90 million random bit
patterns; \f(CW\*(C`t/drop_duplicates.t\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`t/merge.t\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`t/value_counts.t\*(C'\fR now group
tens of thousands of doubles both ways and require the two answers to match.
.PP
Two further changes in \f(CW\*(C`drop_duplicates\*(C'\fR alone:
.IP \(bu 4
Its interning table started at 64 slots and doubled, so a pass over 10,000
distinct rows rehashed nine times, each one a scattered walk over a table too
big for L2. The row count is known before the pass starts and bounds the group
count, so it is now used as the hint — capped, so a large frame of few distinct
rows does not pay for a slot per row.
.IP \(bu 4
An HoA result copied every surviving cell, while AoA and AoH already shared the
whole surviving row. It now shares the cells too. \fBThis is a behaviour
change.\fR The frame, and an HoA\*(Aqs column arrays, are still new, so they can be
reshaped without touching the input; but assigning \fIthrough\fR a survivor —
\&\f(CW\*(C`$out\->{col}[0] = ...\*(C'\fR — now writes to the input\*(Aqs cell, exactly as
\&\f(CW\*(C`$out\->[0]{col} = ...\*(C'\fR always did for AoA and AoH. Clone the result if you need
full independence.
.PP
Measured on the 10,000\-row frame \f(CW\*(C`benchmark.pl\*(C'\fR uses (five columns: two doubles,
one integer, two strings), on one machine, with only these paths toggled. Time is
the median of 25 calls in one process; RAM is \f(CW\*(C`benchmark.pl\*(C'\fR\*(Aqs own figure, the
\&\f(CW\*(C`VmRSS\*(C'\fR delta of a forked child running the call once, median of nine. The string
row is there to show where the win is not: it is confined to numeric cells.
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`group_by\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`pivot_table\*(C'\fR were left alone: \f(CW\*(C`group_by\*(C'\fR hands the cell SV
straight to \f(CW\*(C`hv_fetch_ent\*(C'\fR, so perl does the stringification internally and
reaching it means byte\-level \f(CW\*(C`hv_*\*(C'\fR calls and a change to how UTF\-8 keys are
handled, and \f(CW\*(C`pivot_table\*(C'\fR is pure Perl.
