.IX Subsection "0.27 2026-07-26 CDT"
New \f(CW\*(C`h\*(C'\fR function: \f(CWh(\*(Aqagg\*(Aq)\fR, \f(CWh(*agg)\fR or \f(CWh(\e&agg)\fR prints that function\*(Aqs section of this document and returns, in the spirit of R\*(Aqs \f(CW\*(C`?function\*(C'\fR. \f(CWh()\fR lists every documented function. It covers the XS functions as well as the Perl ones, because it looks the name up in the module\*(Aqs POD instead of reading an argument list — see "Getting help".
\&\- The pure Perl functions also accept \f(CW\*(Aq?\*(Aq\fR or \f(CW\*(Aqh\*(Aq\fR in place of their arguments, which prints the same text and then dies. \f(CW\*(C`$Stats::LikeR::HELP = 0\*(C'\fR switches that off for code that has to pass a column or file really named \f(CW\*(Aqh\*(Aq\fR.
\&\- \f(CW\*(C`qcut\*(C'\fR\*(Aqs hand\-written usage message was replaced by its section of this document; \f(CWqcut(\*(Aqh\*(Aq)\fR and \f(CWqcut(\*(Aq?\*(Aq)\fR still die, but \f(CWqcut(\*(AqH\*(Aq)\fR no longer means help.
